  "description": "Applies the corpus's own O2 obstruction (compact-quotient neutrality, docs/audits/2026-08-01-em-linking-reads-round1.md) to the kappa(A) hypothesis contest it constrains, which no prior probe had done (bean qou-17mq, todo since 2026-08-01). O2 forces the admissible pair kernel to be the ZERO-MEAN Green's function coth(alpha) - c0 with c0 = <coth>_M > 1, so the unsubtracted coth that H_coth is scored on is not an admissible member of the family, and its winning qualitative prediction -- saturation at kappa -> +1 -- is a property of the excluded c0 = 0 member. This re-scores the SAME committed kappa series under the admissible family. Nothing is fitted beyond the single scale H_coth already carries; the scan over c0 is declared as an extra DOF and is reported as the family's best case, not as support.",
  "auditOnly": "docs/audits/2026-08-01-em-linking-reads-round1.md",
  "data": {
    "obstruction": {
      "name": "O2 -- compact-quotient neutrality",
      "source": "docs/audits/2026-08-01-em-linking-reads-round1.md (round 2)",
      "statement": "int(Laplacian u) = 0 on a closed manifold forces total charge zero; the Green's function acquires a -1/vol(M) offset and only charge-neutral combinations are well-posed.",
      "consequence_for_the_kernel": "The admissible pair kernel is the zero-mean Green's function coth(alpha) - c0 with c0 = <coth>_M. Since coth > 1 pointwise on (0, inf), c0 > 1 strictly for any finite-volume M; c0 = 1 is the infinite-volume BOUNDARY of the family, not an interior member. The unsubtracted coth is c0 = 0 and is outside the admissible family entirely.",
      "sign_change_is_forced": "The robust form of the argument, independent of any model of the compact Green's function: an admissible kernel has zero mean over M and is not identically zero, so it MUST take both signs. coth(alpha) is strictly positive and monotone, so no admissible kernel is a positive saturating function of the separation. Physically this is ordinary jellium behaviour -- a like-charge pair against a neutralising background is repulsive at short range and attractive beyond a critical separation. The single-term model coth(alpha) - c0 used for the scan below is the simplest realisation of that; the sign-change conclusion does not depend on it.",
      "finite_volume_suffices": "int(Laplacian u) = 0 needs finite volume, not compactness, so the argument covers the corpus's cusped finite-volume hyperbolic knot complements (4_1, L6a4) as well as a closed quotient. The audit states the QOU fibre is a compact hyperbolic quotient; this probe takes that premise as given and notes it is stronger than the argument needs.",
      "consequence_for_the_contest": "H_coth's distinguishing prediction is saturation at kappa -> +1. Every admissible member instead has kappa -> -c0 <= -1. So the qualitative behaviour that separated H_coth from the power laws is not a prediction of any admissible kernel."
    },
